From 55e0765f9fba6712a28e713b5405c1218a3e880e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 15:42:10 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] logging: structure concrete wallet startup and storage
 diagnostics

Give all nine concrete direct Info sites stable events: wallet-directory
selection/scanning, SQLite close failure, cursor failures and partial key
decryption. Preserve original severity, readable text, database return values,
recursion policy and exceptions. No key, passphrase, SQL data or wallet record
contents are added. The variadic WalletLogPrintf helper remains separately
reviewed infrastructure work, not falsely counted as a converted consumer.

A focused POSIX non-root functional control uses an owned empty walletdir,
checks an unreadable child remains a nonfatal listwalletdir result, restores
permissions in finally, and checks actual startup/scan records after clean
stop. Runtime and rare cursor/close/decryption failures are not claimed yet.

Scripted diff (ast-grep-py0.51.0; reviewed per-site catalog):
/private/tmp/lane-n4-build/logging-compose/ast-venv/bin/python contrib/logging/conversion/convert.py --root . --rules contrib/logging/conversion/rules/wallet-direct-diagnostics.json --report /Users/shammah/repos/lotus-v2-repair-work/logging-cleanup/wallet350-conversion.json --apply
git clang-format --force --binary /opt/homebrew/bin/clang-format --style '{BasedOnStyle: InheritParentConfig, BreakStringLiterals: false}' HEAD -- src/wallet/load.cpp src/wallet/sqlite.cpp src/wallet/walletdb.cpp src/wallet/scriptpubkeyman.cpp src/wallet/walletutil.cpp

The two partial-decryption calls intentionally share an event; their distinct
literal-split AST fingerprints have separate legacy/descriptor rule IDs.
Initial duplicate-ID catalog attempts failed closed before any source write;
the corrected catalog applies all nine sites atomically. Native gate pending.

